{"command": "cd /testbed && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\ncontent = \"\"\"# cachetools Constitution\n<!-- Project: cachetools (milestone 1: cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache) -->\n\n## Sync Impact Report\n<!-- Temporary scratch for human review of this amendment; remove before commit. -->\n- Version change: (none, unversioned scaffold) -> 1.0.0\n- Modified principles: scaffold placeholders -> five adopted principles\n  - [PRINCIPLE_1_NAME] -> I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\n  - [PRINCIPLE_2_NAME] -> II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\n  - [PRINCIPLE_3_NAME] -> III. Evidence Over Assertion\n  - [PRINCIPLE_4_NAME] -> IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\n  - [PRINCIPLE_5_NAME] -> V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\n- Added sections: Development Workflow (new); Governance rules concretized\n- Removed sections: none\n- Follow-up TODOs: none\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\nAll existing `cachetools` public APIs MUST remain importable, callable, and\nbehaviorally unchanged. New functionality MUST be additive (for example, the\nnew `cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache` type) and MUST NOT alter, shadow, or\nremove existing names, signatures, or semantics. Upstream test files MUST\nremain unmodified; any observed behavior change in existing APIs is a defect\nand MUST be reported as a regression before merging.\nRationale: this is a library milestone layered on a maintained package;\ndownstream code relies on the current contract, so additions are safe only\nwhile the existing surface is byte-for-byte stable.\n\n### II. Testable Acceptance Criteria\nEvery requirement MUST state at least one concrete, observable, testable\nacceptance criterion (input, action, expected output or exception). Vague\nlanguage (\"should\", \"fast\", \"clean\") MUST NOT define acceptance. Each\nrequirement MUST be verifiable by a test or a recorded command whose output\ncan be inspected, and the public acceptance suite `acceptance_public.py`\nMUST pass unmodified. Candidate extensions (for example, the Claim-A\n`put_no_recency_refresh` variant) MUST be recorded explicitly as extensions\nand MUST NOT silently alter the base requirement text.\nRationale: autonomous phases cannot ask for clarification; only\nmachine-checkable criteria keep later phases convergent.\n\n### III. Evidence Over Assertion\nClaims of completion MUST cite observed evidence: a test command with its\nexit status and output, or an inspected artifact. Unverified expectations\nMUST be labeled as assumptions, not facts. Hidden or unavailable acceptance\nevidence MUST NOT be claimed as executed. Distinguish in every handoff\nbetween (a) observed, (b) inferred, and (c) unverified.\nRationale: fabricated or assumed test results poison later phases; evidence\nis the only transferable state between phases.\n\n### IV. Simple, Scoped Implementations\nPrefer the smallest implementation that satisfies the stated requirements\nwithin the declared scope (for milestone 1: `src/cachetools/tagged.py` and\nits own tests). Reuse existing components (for example, `cachetools.LRUCache`\nfor bounded storage) instead of reimplementing them. No new dependencies,\nno speculative features, no refactoring of unrelated code. Any added\ncomplexity MUST be justified in writing against a stated requirement.\nRationale: scope creep and gratuitous complexity are the main failure modes\nof autonomous implementation; reuse also reduces regression risk on the\npreserved public API.\n\n### V. Documented Assumptions and Regressions\nUnresolved assumptions, open questions, and known regressions MUST be\nwritten down where the next phase will see them (`HANDOFF.md` and the\nfeature docs under `specs/`). Each item MUST state what is assumed, what\nevidence would confirm or refute it, and what decision it blocks. A\nregression MUST be recorded the moment it is observed, with the command\nthat reproduces it.\nRationale: conversation history does not survive across phases; written\nassumptions and regressions are the only durable record.\n\n## Development Workflow\n- Feature documents live in `specs/001-transactions/` (feature directory\n  `specs/001-transactions`); keep them concise and keep every claim\n  evidence-explicit.\n- Phase order is fixed: constitution -> specify -> plan -> tasks ->\n  implement. The constitution phase MUST NOT create or modify application\n  source, tests, or deployment artifacts; it writes only this file.\n- Implementation is deferred to later phases and MUST target\n  `src/cachetools/tagged.py`; its own tests MAY be added, but upstream tests\n  and `acceptance_public.py` MUST remain unchanged.\n- Each phase MUST end with a completion report that references the artifacts\n  it produced and the commands it ran.\n\n## Governance\n- This constitution supersedes all other project practices and prior design\n  notes; where older notes conflict with it, the constitution wins.\n- Amendments: edit `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, update the Sync Impact\n  Report, bump the version, and record the rationale in the completion\n  report. No other files are amended by a constitution change.\n- Versioning: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH. MAJOR for removed or redefined\n  principles; MINOR for added principles or materially expanded guidance;\n  PATCH for wording, typos, and non-semantic clarifications.\n- Compliance review: before a phase is marked done, verify that its\n  artifacts satisfy the principles above and that all claims carry observed\n  evidence; violations MUST be fixed or recorded as documented exceptions\n  with a follow-up item.\n- Ratification: 2026-10-17, by the approved principle inputs supplied for\n  this autonomous benchmark (milestone 1, cachetools).\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-10-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-10-17\n\"\"\"\npath = \"/testbed/.specify/memory/constitution.md\"\nwith open(path, \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\nprint(\"written\", len(content), \"chars\")\nPYEOF\necho ===; grep -nE '\\[[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]+\\]' /